<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY13-QA-008>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY13-QA-008" ;
  triage:title "ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-F001: doctor_projection.rs re-derives the all-teams-vs-single-team fact instead of consuming atm-core's already-resolved DoctorTeamScope decision" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1300-r1 (PR #1300, AY.13 doctor team scope). StorageDoctorProjection::project computes `let team_context = !report.team_rosters.is_empty();` to re-derive the scope fact from raw data shape instead of consuming the scope decision atm-core already resolved for this run. atm-core computes the authoritative decision as DoctorTeamScope (crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs, or team_scope.rs post-split) and carries only a display string (DoctorReport.team_scope: String) across the crate seam; the enum and its is_all_teams()/report_name() accessors are private to atm-core::doctor and never reach atm-runtime. This is safe today only because of an unenforced, implicit invariant in load_scoped_rosters that member_roster and team_rosters are always mutually exclusive by construction; nothing prevents that invariant from silently breaking in a future change, at which point doctor_projection.rs would silently misattribute or drop team-scoped Herdr presence findings. Confirmed still present after the r2 doctor/mod.rs->team_scope.rs split (delta did not touch doctor_projection.rs)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary-violation" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-runtime/src/doctor_projection.rs, crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs, crates/atm-core/src/doctor/team_scope.rs, crates/atm-core/src/doctor/report.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-07T17:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-07T17:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
